{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "title": "No generation to split on",
    "subtitle": "A package of twenty-six functions, with nothing between the package and them"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "origin": "handwritten",
    "note": "Written to hold the one page shape nothing else covers: wide. Go's hierarchy has a file generation between a package and its functions, and a language without one gives stage 3 nothing to split a package on, so every function becomes a column. The thin page beside it is the control, and the two fail to split for opposite reasons: three members is under the unfold window, so the unfold is tried and finds leaves to give it nothing; twenty-six is over the window, so the unfold is never tried at all. Measured rather than supposed, and docs/decisions.md records what the measurement corrected."
  },
